  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "One given name, sometimes two, then one family name inherited from the father; since 2022 a child can also carry the mother's. Women keep their own family name when they marry. Family names are often regional: Esposito is Neapolitan, Brambilla and Colombo are Lombard, Rossi is everywhere. At work and on forms the family name often comes first (Rossi Marco). Milan has the country's largest immigrant communities: Egyptian, Filipino, Chinese (mostly from Zhejiang, often using an Italian name day to day), Peruvian, Romanian, Albanian, Moroccan and Sri Lankan.",
